# `Object.defineProperties(Taker.prototype, { wide: taken.wide })`, taken = a map of descriptors that another body has written and laid whole on Source.prototype.
# The map has been handed to native code, so in the reading in which unseen code does anything it is lost, and nothing is expected there. What is held knows its layout, and the records go by what is held.
# RUN(WIDE): link members held mechanisms=all
# WIDE: on-prototype L0 "wide" getter=f5
# RUN(DEEP): link members held mechanisms=all
# DEEP: on-prototype L0 "deep" getter=f6 setter=f7
# RUN(LOST): link members mechanisms=all
# LOST-NOT: on-prototype L0 "wide" getter=
# RUN(MAP): summary f0
# MAP: Define {{*}}"wide" {{*}}accessor-as-written getter=f5 in-map=L
# RUN(TAKEN): summary f3
# TAKEN: Define {{*}}"wide" {{*}}descriptor-from=
# PROGRAM-OF: ../answers/an-accessor-laid-by-a-descriptor-out-of-a-map-is-found-while-the-guards-hold.ir
